# The root is a read-only squashfs; everything that is written lives in a tmpfs
# and is gone at power off. That is the trade the image makes: nothing to fsck
# on a card that loses power with the ignition.
#
# /log is the exception, and it is the one partition that is written: a FAT
# holding what the boot had to say about itself. It is a separate partition
# rather than a file on the boot one so that a card pulled mid-write cannot
# damage what U-Boot reads, and it is FAT so that it mounts on a laptop with the
# card in a reader.
/dev/root	/		squashfs	ro,noatime		0 0
tmpfs		/tmp		tmpfs		mode=1777		0 0
tmpfs		/run		tmpfs		mode=0755		0 0
tmpfs		/var/log	tmpfs		mode=0755,size=4M	0 0
/dev/mmcblk0p3	/log		vfat		rw,noatime,umask=0022	0 0
